{"1-10":{"people":[{"id":"esau-h6215g","name":"Esau","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":3,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"isaac-h3327","name":"Isaac","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":2,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"rebekah-h7259","name":"Rebekah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Laban","count":2,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":6}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H4303","lemma":"מַטְעָם","tr":"mat·am","gloss":"delicacy","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":8},{"base":"H6215","lemma":"עֵשָׂו","tr":"e·sav","gloss":"Esau","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":97},{"base":"H9030","lemma":"נִי","tr":"ni","gloss":"me","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":908},{"base":"H6718","lemma":"צַ֫יִד","tr":"tsa·yid","gloss":"wild game","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":19},{"base":"H4194","lemma":"מָ֫וֶת","tr":"ma·vet","gloss":"death","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":155},{"base":"H6679","lemma":"צוּד","tr":"tsud","gloss":"to hunt","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":18},{"base":"H1288","lemma":"בָּרַךְ","tr":"ba·rakh","gloss":"to bless","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":330},{"base":"H2204","lemma":"זָקֵן","tr":"za·qen","gloss":"be old","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":27},{"base":"H7259","lemma":"רִבְקָה","tr":"riv·qah","gloss":"Rebekah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":30},{"base":"H4994","lemma":"נָא","tr":"na","gloss":"please","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":404}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":48,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Now Israelʼs eyesight was poor because of old age; he could hardly see. Joseph brought his sons to him, and his father kissed them and embraced them.","from":1},{"book":"HEB","chapter":11,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"By faith Isaac blessed Jacob and Esau concerning the future.","from":4},{"book":"1SA","chapter":3,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"And at that time Eli, whose eyesight had grown so dim that he could not see, was lying in his room.","from":1},{"book":"GEN","chapter":48,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Joseph said to his father, “They are the sons God has given me in this place.” So Jacob said, “Please bring them to me, that I may bless them.”","from":4},{"book":"GEN","chapter":25,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"When the boys grew up, Esau became a skillful hunter, a man of the field, while Jacob was a quiet man who stayed at home.","from":3},{"book":"GEN","chapter":25,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"Because Isaac had a taste for wild game, he loved Esau; but Rebekah loved Jacob.","from":3},{"book":"GEN","chapter":27,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"“Serve me,” said Isaac, “and let me eat some of my sonʼs game, so that I may bless you.” Jacob brought it to him, and he ate; then he brought him wine, and he drank.","from":4},{"book":"GEN","chapter":49,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"These are the tribes of Israel, twelve in all, and this was what their father said to them. He blessed them, and he blessed each one with a suitable blessing.","from":4}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":4}]},"11-17":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":3,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"esau-h6215g","name":"Esau","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"rebekah-h7259","name":"Rebekah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Laban","count":2,"firstVerse":11}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H0517","lemma":"אֵם","tr":"em","gloss":"mother","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":220},{"base":"H4303","lemma":"מַטְעָם","tr":"mat·am","gloss":"delicacy","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":8},{"base":"H3290","lemma":"יַעֲקֹב","tr":"ya·a·qov","gloss":"Jacob","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":350},{"base":"H7259","lemma":"רִבְקָה","tr":"riv·qah","gloss":"Rebekah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":30},{"base":"H7045","lemma":"קְלָלָה","tr":"qe·la·lah","gloss":"curse","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":33},{"base":"H6215","lemma":"עֵשָׂו","tr":"e·sav","gloss":"Esau","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":97},{"base":"H3847","lemma":"לָבֵשׁ","tr":"la·vash","gloss":"to clothe","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":110},{"base":"H3947","lemma":"לָקַח","tr":"la·qach","gloss":"to take: take","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":966},{"base":"H8591","lemma":"תָּעַע","tr":"ta·a","gloss":"to mock","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H2509","lemma":"חָלָק","tr":"cha·laq","gloss":"smooth","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":27,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"So he came near and kissed him. When Isaac smelled his clothing, he blessed him and said: “Ah, the smell of my son is like the smell of a field that the Lordhas blessed.","from":15},{"book":"GEN","chapter":25,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"The first one came out red, covered with hair like a fur coat; so they named him Esau.","from":11},{"book":"MAT","chapter":27,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"All the people answered, “His blood be on us and on our children!”","from":13},{"book":"DEU","chapter":27,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"‘Cursed is he who lets a blind man wander in the road.’ And let all the people say, ‘Amen!’","from":12},{"book":"GEN","chapter":9,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"he said, “Cursed be Canaan! A servant of servants shall he be to his brothers.”","from":12},{"book":"GEN","chapter":25,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and He declared to her: “Two nations are in your womb, and two peoples from within you will be separated; one people will be stronger than the other, and the older will serve the younger.”","from":13},{"book":"GEN","chapter":25,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When the boys grew up, Esau became a skillful hunter, a man of the field, while Jacob was a quiet man who stayed at home.","from":12},{"book":"GEN","chapter":25,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Because Isaac had a taste for wild game, he loved Esau; but Rebekah loved Jacob.","from":14}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]},"18-29":{"people":[{"id":"esau-h6215g","name":"Esau","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":5,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":3,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"isaac-h3327","name":"Isaac","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":4,"firstVerse":20}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H5066","lemma":"נָגַשׁ","tr":"na·gash","gloss":"to approach: approach","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":125},{"base":"H1288","lemma":"בָּרַךְ","tr":"ba·rakh","gloss":"to bless","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":330},{"base":"H6215","lemma":"עֵשָׂו","tr":"e·sav","gloss":"Esau","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":97},{"base":"H3327","lemma":"יִצְחָק","tr":"yits·chaq","gloss":"Isaac","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":108},{"base":"H7381","lemma":"רֵיחַ","tr":"re·ach","gloss":"aroma","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":58},{"base":"H3290","lemma":"יַעֲקֹב","tr":"ya·a·qov","gloss":"Jacob","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":350},{"base":"H6718","lemma":"צַ֫יִד","tr":"tsa·yid","gloss":"wild game","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":19},{"base":"H4994","lemma":"נָא","tr":"na","gloss":"please","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":404},{"base":"H5401","lemma":"נָשַׁק","tr":"na·shaq","gloss":"to kiss","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":35},{"base":"H0779","lemma":"אָרַר","tr":"a·rar","gloss":"to curse","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":63}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"I will bless those who bless you and curse those who curse you; and all the families of the earth will be blessed through you.”","from":29},{"book":"NUM","chapter":24,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"He crouches, he lies down like a lion; like a lioness, who dares to rouse him? Blessed are those who bless you and cursed are those who curse you.”","from":29},{"book":"DEU","chapter":33,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"So Israel dwells securely; the fountain of Jacob lives untroubled in a land of grain and new wine, where even the heavens drip with dew.","from":28},{"book":"ISA","chapter":49,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"Kings will be your foster fathers, and their queens your nursing mothers. They will bow to you facedown and lick the dust at your feet. Then you will know that I am the LORD; those who hope in Me will never be put to shame.”","from":29},{"book":"HEB","chapter":6,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"For land that drinks in the rain often falling on it and that produces a crop useful to those for whom it is tended receives the blessing of God.","from":27},{"book":"DEU","chapter":33,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Concerning Joseph he said: “May his land be blessed by the LORD with the precious dew from heaven above and the deep waters that lie beneath,","from":28},{"book":"PSA","chapter":65,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"You soak its furrows and level its ridges; You soften it with showers and bless its growth.","from":27},{"book":"GEN","chapter":9,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"he said, “Cursed be Canaan! A servant of servants shall he be to his brothers.”","from":29}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]},"30-40":{"people":[{"id":"esau-h6215g","name":"Esau","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":5,"firstVerse":30},{"id":"isaac-h3327","name":"Isaac","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":5,"firstVerse":30},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":30}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H1062","lemma":"בְּכֹרָה","tr":"be·kho·rah","gloss":"birthright","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10,"top":true},{"base":"H6215","lemma":"עֵשָׂו","tr":"e·sav","gloss":"Esau","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":97},{"base":"H3327","lemma":"יִצְחָק","tr":"yits·chaq","gloss":"Isaac","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":108},{"base":"H1288","lemma":"בָּרַךְ","tr":"ba·rakh","gloss":"to bless","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":330},{"base":"H1293","lemma":"בְּרָכָה","tr":"be·ra·khah","gloss":"blessing","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":69},{"base":"H6718","lemma":"צַ֫יִד","tr":"tsa·yid","gloss":"wild game","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":19},{"base":"H0251","lemma":"אָח","tr":"ach","gloss":"brother: male-sibling","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":629},{"base":"H1571","lemma":"גַּם","tr":"gam","gloss":"also","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":769},{"base":"H0645","lemma":"אֵפוֹ","tr":"e·pho","gloss":"then","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":15},{"base":"H3290","lemma":"יַעֲקֹב","tr":"ya·a·qov","gloss":"Jacob","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":350},{"base":"H0589","lemma":"אֲנִי","tr":"a·ni","gloss":"I","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":874}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2KI","chapter":8,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"In the days of Jehoram, Edom rebelled against the hand of Judah and appointed their own king.","from":40},{"book":"2KI","chapter":8,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"So to this day Edom has been in rebellion against the hand of Judah. Likewise, Libnah rebelled at the same time.","from":40},{"book":"GEN","chapter":25,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"After this, his brother came out grasping Esauʼs heel; so he was named Jacob. And Isaac was sixty years old when the twins were born.","from":36},{"book":"GEN","chapter":27,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"May God give to you the dew of heaven and the richness of the earth— an abundance of grain and new wine.","from":39},{"book":"HEB","chapter":12,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"For you know that afterward, when he wanted to inherit the blessing, he was rejected. He could find no ground for repentance, though he sought the blessing with tears.","from":34},{"book":"GEN","chapter":25,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"and He declared to her: “Two nations are in your womb, and two peoples from within you will be separated; one people will be stronger than the other, and the older will serve the younger.”","from":40},{"book":"GEN","chapter":28,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"May God Almighty bless you and make you fruitful and multiply you, so that you may become a company of peoples.","from":33},{"book":"GEN","chapter":28,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"And may He give the blessing of Abraham to you and your descendants, so that you may possess the land where you dwell as a foreigner, the land God gave to Abraham.”","from":33}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]},"41-46":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":3,"firstVerse":41},{"id":"esau-h6215g","name":"Esau","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":41},{"id":"rebekah-h7259","name":"Rebekah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Laban","count":2,"firstVerse":42},{"id":"laban-h3837a","name":"Laban","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Bethuel","count":1,"firstVerse":43},{"id":"heth-h2845","name":"Heth","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Canaan","count":1,"firstVerse":46},{"id":"isaac-h3327","name":"Isaac","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":1,"firstVerse":46}],"places":[{"id":"haran-h2771a","name":"Haran","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":43}],"words":[{"base":"H6215","lemma":"עֵשָׂו","tr":"e·sav","gloss":"Esau","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":97},{"base":"H0251","lemma":"אָח","tr":"ach","gloss":"brother: male-sibling","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":629},{"base":"H3290","lemma":"יַעֲקֹב","tr":"ya·a·qov","gloss":"Jacob","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":350},{"base":"H2845","lemma":"חֵת","tr":"chet","gloss":"Heth","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":14},{"base":"H7259","lemma":"רִבְקָה","tr":"riv·qah","gloss":"Rebekah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":30},{"base":"H1323","lemma":"בַּת","tr":"bat","gloss":"daughter","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":588},{"base":"H2026","lemma":"הָרַג","tr":"ha·rag","gloss":"to kill","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":167},{"base":"H2416","lemma":"חַי","tr":"chay","gloss":"alive","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":498},{"base":"H7852","lemma":"שָׂטַם","tr":"sa·tam","gloss":"to hate","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H9031","lemma":"ךָּ","tr":"ka","gloss":"you","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":727}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":37,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"When Josephʼs brothers saw that their father loved him more than any of them, they hated him and could not speak a kind word to him.","from":41},{"book":"1JN","chapter":3,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Do not be like Cain, who belonged to the evil one and murdered his brother. And why did Cain slay him? Because his own deeds were evil, while those of his brother were righteous.","from":41},{"book":"1JN","chapter":3,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Everyone who hates his brother is a murderer, and you know that eternal life does not reside in a murderer.","from":41},{"book":"GEN","chapter":24,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"and I will have you swear by the Lord, the God of heaven and the God of earth, that you will not take a wife for my son from the daughters of the Canaanites among whom I am dwelling,","from":46},{"book":"GEN","chapter":26,"verse":34,"verseEnd":34,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"When Esau was forty years old, he took as his wives Judith daughter of Beeri the Hittite and Basemath daughter of Elon the Hittite.","from":46},{"book":"GEN","chapter":26,"verse":35,"verseEnd":35,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"And they brought grief to Isaac and Rebekah.","from":46},{"book":"GEN","chapter":50,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"taking the forty days required to complete the embalming. And the Egyptians mourned for him seventy days.","from":41},{"book":"GEN","chapter":50,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"When the days of mourning had passed, Joseph said to Pharaohʼs court, “If I have found favor in your eyes, please tell Pharaoh that","from":41}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":5}]}}